.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:232:3. A gpt-6-luna route with a table entry → `{ bounded, ms, source: 'route_table:<evidence D-id>' }`.
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:233:4. A gpt-6-luna route without an entry → throws `gpt-6-luna <effort> <path> has no measured session budget (LUNA6 pilot); pass --timeout-ms`.
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:235:Escalation sessions use the same `config.timeoutMs` as the base route (`:4215`). So if the Q1 answer gives escalation a route whose budget differs from the base (only (b) max does), the resolver must also resolve the escalation route and throw when the two differ, the same as the mixed-arm rule below. Arena runs with several `--arm`s resolve each arm. If the resolved budgets differ and no explicit value was given, the run throws, because one shared budget would be a confound. The runners print the resolved `{timeoutMs, source}` at start. Wrappers copy that line and `--timeout-ms` into their launch provenance JSON, which is where budgets are recorded (D887). The effort type is a type-only import of `ConversationEffort`, so no runtime import cost is added.
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:237:### 3.4 Pilot (supervisor-run; quiet box per D883; never re-pinned for load)
