.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:253:- **Censoring (r1 P1-3).** The pilot timeout is **T = 1,800 s**, 2× the longest codex session ever seen in `~/.codex-aidm` (902.7 s [V-r0]). The draft's 900 s was below that maximum. The rule is fixed before P1: **if any session in an arm/path reaches T, that arm/path's budget is withheld** and the owner is told. No budget is ever derived from a censored sample. After the second T-hit, that arm/path stops early to save wall time.
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:254:- **Budget rule (fixed before P1).** Take the pooled n = 40 sample and its nearest-rank p95, which is the 38th order statistic [V: `ceil(0.95·40) = 38`]. The budget is the smallest multiple of 30 s that is ≥ 1.25 × p95. Stability check: if the day-1-only p95 (29th of 30) and the pooled p95 differ by more than 20 %, the budget is withheld. The report states the fraction of pilot sessions the budget would have cut. With n = 40, the p95 rests on 2-3 order statistics, and the report says so.
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:256:- **Cost and wall.** Usage is codex-plan only [V-r0]. Wall time is at least 6.65 h serial if xhigh ≈ gpt-5.6-luna high's 162 s, or about 12.1 h if xhigh takes twice as long [I; node arithmetic, Appendix A]. It runs over two days because of the day-2 slice.
