.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:334:## 5. DATA-01
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:336:### 5.1 Arithmetic (the reviewer's reproduction is accepted; one correction from the DATA-01 triage)
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:338:The reviewer reproduced the break-evens: `$500 / 33,801 = $0.01479246` (max pilot) and `$500 / 5,801 = $0.08619204` [V: node]. The 5,801-request **minimum pilot is unattainable** under DATA-01's own stopping rule. A unanimous leader cannot separate at n = 5 for any K ≥ 2 (0.5⁵ = 0.03125 > 0.0125), so the floor is 9,801 requests at n = 10 or 17,801 at n = 20. This is from the triage agent (D887 wave 1; `.tmp/runs/perf-02/fanout/triage-data-01/result.md`) [R]. The draft's "min pilot" and "boundaries after min pilot" columns are therefore void and are dropped. The fix r3 schedule replaces them.
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:344:| gpt-5.6-luna ($0.20 / $1.20 per M) | 8k | $0.0120 | $405.61 | 81.12 % | $213.61 |
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:348:| gpt-6-luna per reviewer ($0.10 / $0.50 per M, **UNVERIFIED**) | 8k | $0.0052 | $175.77 | 35.15 % | $92.57 |
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:353:The reviewer's gpt-6-luna prices come from its own web read of the model page. I could not verify them, because this round has no network.
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:357:- **pricingVersion pins more than the model.** It must record the model snapshot, the processing tier (standard, batch or priority), the region, the API route, the fetch date and the source URL, all from a primary source. One mismatch at the route probe stops the pilot.
.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:358:- **Mandatory headroom.** D841's $500 includes retries and ambiguous holds, so the break-even must hold with headroom: `r ≤ (500 − H) / N_max`, where H is the declared retry and hold reserve. For example, H = 10 % gives r ≤ $0.01331322, and H = 20 % gives r ≤ $0.01183397 [V: node]. DATA-01 fix r3 chooses and justifies H. A pilot is authorized only if the probe-measured r satisfies this inequality under the revised schedule's N_max.
