.claude/decisions.md:64:- A queue uses either exit-file ordering or process-presence checks, not both; sleeping queued waiters are not machine load. Queue controllers never write the gate log they await. [D586.83/D611.2]
.claude/decisions.md:79:- (owner) Run gates while independent lanes continue; each timeout-red gets exactly ONE serial rerun (`--no-file-parallelism`) before counting. Report both outcomes, never assume retry cause, and never re-pin budgets for load. Quiet same-box runs remain mandatory for performance evidence. [D264/D587.3/D586.77/D632/D644]
.claude/decisions.md:82:  D635.32: only “is versioned, uses generic classic-board conventions, and leaks no non-rendered probe identity” at `tests/unit/tools/ai-dm-screenshot-probe.test.ts:464`, 5,000 → 10,000 ms; cost reduction stays queued. All other budgets remain fixed. [D544/D584.25/D606/D613/D635.32]
.claude/decisions.md:86:- (owner) No assertions weakened, waits added, skip/todo/ignore/any escapes introduced or config changed merely for green. Generation during module collection before timeouts apply is budget evasion; fix performance within budget or stop with measurements. [D7/D9/D25/D586.60/F: browser regression investigation, 2026-09-08/D576@2026-09-08T04:55]
.claude/decisions.md:88:- Every load-bearing assertion needs a named compiling runtime mutation and exact killer; type-rejected mutants prove no runtime behavior. Scripts fail loudly on missing targets, print changed lines/counts, and verify the mutant reaches the tested surface. [F25/F: runtime mutation evidence, 2026-09-03/F: mutation script guards, 2026-09-03/RULES.md: COMMON RULES]
.claude/decisions.md:89:- Mutation scripts restore exact bytes in the same script, write RESTORED, then rerun killers; untracked files require explicit backups. Never mutate during a gate on that tree; never `git checkout -- <path>` over uncommitted lane work. [F28/F: new-file mutation restoration, 2026-09-02/F: mutant restoration, 2026-09-06]
.claude/decisions.md:90:- (owner) Surviving mutants go in commit and decision records with required next-increment killing test; ordinary survivor alone does not block landing. The explicit release mutation bar remains separately binding. [D539/D391.2]
.claude/decisions.md:91:- (owner) Fresh full mutation audits include static mutants; iterative shard reruns use ignoreStatic and the per-shard incremental cache, reporting skipped counts UNMEASURED. Classify survivors as killed/compile-error/equivalent with proof/explicitly excluded; ordinary constructible inputs define reachability. [D280/D282/D308/D310/D334.3]
