.claude/decisions.md:954:Fix r1 (resumed sol, 401,779 tokens cumulative): PcRosterStub {id, name, side}; ActorLocalEncounterState with request-boundary and ActorLocalCapsuleView companions (closes astra P1: no producer receives EngineStateCapsule); brand = non-exported classes with private `#brand` fields plus issuance WeakSets, compile witnesses for spread forgery and actor rebinding (P2-A); frozen-core seam resolves the original WeakMap-authenticated registered offers with an instrumented regeneration count of exactly 0 (P2-B); producer closure 19 → 25 families incl. snippet registry, plays/skills/suggestions, revision summaries, journal URIs and 48-char cursors on actor-safe digests; submission contract exposes only actor-local results or typed withheld receipts (P2-D); 12 batches ≤ 10 files, union 56 (22 source/tool, 1 generated schema per D596, 33 tests) (P2-C); D583 218 sha f5bf19bd…; probes retained (Wizard HALF/HALF, context 95a90763…, generation audit 1 sentinel / 0 forbidden with the config source now in the plan). It still REMOVES monster images (plan ~:158, B7), which D753 supersedes; amendment r1b dispatched on the same session (brief `plan-boundary-fix-r1b.md`: actor-local PNG/HTML producer on the boundary type, image-byte relocation invariance + positive-draw + structural-DOM witnesses, three image mutants, B7 reworked, union and D583 recounted). Astra HIGH r2 follows the amendment. Next free id: D755. (superseded by D755)
.claude/decisions.md:958:Verbatim: "B. Hide the roster from the monster until a character does something to be perceived. Only knows about a pc that has revealed itself" (to "what may a monster say or narrate about a never-perceived PC?"; options A identity-only no claims / B silence / C free). Ruling and consequences, recorded by the supervisor: (1) D694's "contributes only roster identity" is narrowed: a never-perceived PC is ABSENT from the acting monster's world — no roster entry, no name, no count, no stub. The boundary plan's PcRosterStub is deleted; the actor-local state carries only self, allies, perceived opponents and (per D671) indication-revealed opponents; roster/legend/board/narration/capture surfaces list only those. (2) "Revealed itself" = the BLIND-01 actor-knowledge precedence: seen, or an indication (search memory / observation history) — D671 unchanged pending the next question (whether an indication reveals WHICH PC or only that something is there). (3) BLIND-01's landed D693 no-cue mechanism, which emits unseen-opponent visibility dependencies keyed by roster identity ("reveals nothing beyond roster identity"), is now non-compliant and is amended inside D694-INTEL-01: a no-cue posture may not enumerate unseen opponents at all; the planner must design the replacement (e.g. no dependencies for a no-cue typed Dodge, or an identity-free "unknown presence" dependency) and re-derive the affected pins (speculative-planning §7 row; the N3 base rank 3 `visibility:DB:TBP` and both sealed-menu entries referencing P become invalid — COHORT N3 needs an N4 re-derivation after this unit; Batch 9 was already blocked on it). (4) Narration: monster prose may not mention, count or allude to an unperceived PC; witness = narration bytes identical across relocation AND across the unperceived PC's removal from the encounter. (5) Options: BLIND-01 offers never target unperceived PCs (KNOW-F2), unchanged; the typed withheld annotation arm remains for third-party effects. (6) Player-side symmetry is untouched (D694: no reciprocal omniscience). Fed into the plan: amendment r1c on the planning session after r1b lands; astra HIGH r2 follows. Next free id: D756. (superseded by D756)
