.claude/decisions.md:1151:The test-of-the-test mutant did its job (removing the `position_prose_cell` scanner entry made exactly the positive-control test fail: "expected [] to include 'prompt:position_prose_cell'" — a semantic kill of the missing check). But my reversal script asserted the insertion anchor was unique and it was not (the `position_gutter_label` literal occurs more than once in the file), so the reversal aborted and the worktree stayed MUTATED while I dispatched astra r3 — a review started on a dirty tree. Correction within the same minute: the candidate was already COMMITTED (e90c6292), so `git checkout -- <file>` was the correct and safe restore this time (D788's rule is about UNCOMMITTED lane work); the restored file's sha equals the HEAD blob; the r3 lane was killed by PID (wrapper + child), its partial log kept as `review-b3-r3-astra.aborted.log`, and r3 re-dispatched on the clean tree. Lesson added to D788's rule: a reversal script must re-insert by the exact removed text at a unique anchor OR simply restore from the commit when the candidate is committed — and the dispatch of a review must be gated on `git status --short` being empty, printed, not assumed.
