.claude/decisions.md:1287:Astra MEDIUM r1 (`.claude/consensus/d694-intel-01/review-b7-astra-r1.md`, session 01a0c047-0a89-7243-94cc-a8408f374fe1, 96,570 tokens; 50 `claude -p` hits = record quotations). P1 (static derivation, not run): `scoreTeamPlans` (team-scorer.ts:573) takes candidates per actor's cache but aggregates on the FIRST local's mechanics — with asymmetric perception (A blind-Dodges, B attacks a P only B perceives) combined damage looks B's target up in A's world and throws an ordinary `Damage target … is absent.` (option-outcome.ts:708); and `compareAllocations` (:391) REGENERATES options via `availableEngineActorOptions` on that first-local state — a post-boundary regeneration in the wrong projected world; order-dependent. My B7 mutants and witnesses (single-actor / fully perceived) could not expose it — finding against my witness design as well as codex's. P2: `combined_damage_exactness_unresolved` unauthorised (reviewer: §4 does not require it). P3s: the window helper's contiguous-run assumption undocumented/unenforced; several witnesses pass on a uniformly empty report. Confirmed by astra: window semantics, caller closure, D693 removal with B18 correctly deferred (and B18 is a real behaviour gap, not just a stale test), all test removals accounted for, freeze intact. RULINGS: (a) the exactness fallback is REVERTED to the original throw (no plan authorisation; the reviewer agrees); (b) P1 fix must carry each actor's own local through allocation and aggregation, forbid post-boundary regeneration (generation-counter assertion), combine over the SHARED target domain with an explicit typed disposition for out-of-domain contributions citing §4, witnessed through the production frontier path with reversed-order invariance; (c) the window helper stops at the first living monster like the host and rejects a non-contiguous requested set with a typed error; (d) positive retained-candidate assertions added to the vacuous witnesses. Fix r2 dispatched on the re