.claude/decisions.md:1291:Astra HIGH r8 (`.claude/consensus/publish-01/review-plan-astra-r8.md`, session 01a0c045-9145-7070-a206-54a5089d43c0, 122,390 tokens; 17 `claude -p` hits = quotations). The reviewer reproduced the generator output byte-for-byte (18,438 bytes; 193/175; 170/23) and recomputed all 193 keys (with a transport substitution for a sandbox git-stdin stall, policy unchanged). P2-1: the planned rewrite of the command-integrity constant to `srd55-command-integrity-v1` changes an HMAC KEY (integrity.ts:48) used to sign persisted inverse commands, so a private backup restored into the public edition fails signed undo — RULING: retain the bytes by exact exception (the token is only the old basename; nothing secret), with a cross-edition signature witness; re-audit the other rewrites for persisted-format inputs. P2-2: the generator hard-pins the baseline (1,136 blobs / bytes) and prints the SHA into compared output, so it can never pass at publication time (B1 adds robots.txt → 1,137) — RULING: explicit `--audit` (frozen baseline) and `--publish --expect <manifest>` (per-commit selection + reviewed delta file) modes. P2-3: the RTF decoder drops `\cell`/`\row` boundaries and whole `\field` groups (55,900 `\cell`, 17,971 `\row`, a visible hyperlink field in Legal.rtf) — fix decoding, add positive witnesses, regenerate. All other checks confirmed (identity pins, 444-entry seal, PUBLIC-BUILD.txt, witnesses, batches). Fix r8 dispatched on the resumed planning session (`plan-fix-r8.md`); astra r9 follows. These remain mechanical defects under stable rulings; the owner is informed each tick and may stop at any time. Next free id: D833.
