.claude/decisions.md:1307:My first `--audit 8c2219ad` run was refused (`audit commit must be 1218f20e…`): fix r8 re-pinned the frozen baseline to the then-HEAD 1218f20e (ledger line 10 says so; I copied the r7 commit into the r9 brief without re-reading it — finding against my own dispatch hygiene). Rerun `node ledger-gen.mjs --audit 1218f20e`: exit 0, SUMMARY mode=audit total_occurrences=193 total_lines=175 source 185/173/60 archive 8/2/1-of-135 retain=173 rewrite=20 — identical to the ledger's machine block (72 lines vs 71; the only extra line is the heading). SECOND FINDING AGAINST MY OWN WORK: while killing the wrongly-briefed r9 lane I ran `pgrep -f "dispatch-review-plan-r9[.]sh"` in a command whose LATER text contained the literal `dispatch-review-plan-r9.sh` (the redispatch line), so pgrep matched my own shell and the kill loop terminated it (exit 144) before the brief edit, the redispatch and the records ran — exactly the failure the "pkill pattern in own argv" memory warns about; the bracket trick protects only the pattern text, not other occurrences in the same argv. The r9 lane itself was killed as intended. Recovery: brief corrected and redispatched in a command containing no pgrep; verification by log growth, not process match. Next free id: D837.
