.claude/decisions.md:1321:B7 FIX R2 (resumed sol 01a0bfae…, exit 0, 1,130,985 tokens; one `claude -p` hit = the brief; completed BEFORE the limit): committed as 10f99026 (BLOCKED candidate; D788). Codex reports: per-actor local aggregation over the shared target domain (participant intersection of the requested locals), no `compareAllocations`/regeneration on the actor-local path, `damage_target_outside_shared_domain` reason with no numeric vector, aggregation local chosen canonically by actor id (order-invariant), reduced BigInt ledger arithmetic, host path unchanged with its original RangeError, `combined_damage_exactness_unresolved` removed; typed `ActorLocalScenarioWindowError` with stop-at-first-living-monster + requested-run enforcement; positive retained-candidate assertions added; two mutants killed with hashes; all suites as before EXCEPT snippets 36/38: the B8 red plus `snippets.test.ts:369` `frontier_resolution: 'contains_unresolved'` now `fully_resolved`. HARD STOP: that pin predates B1 (present at be09e575:308, introduced by de88050f "Increment 7"), so it is a LONG-STANDING host frontier outcome that fix r2's new arithmetic changes — a behaviour change outside the manifest that codex correctly refused to paper over. Supervisor investigation (why the 3,943,001 frontier was unresolved before, and whether BigInt exactness is a legitimate correction or a widening) in progress; verify-b7-fix-r2 running. Next free id: D840.
.claude/decisions.md:1325:PROBE (my own, out of tree: detached worktree of the cohort branch at /tmp with a mirrored wrapper; probe test saved at `.tmp/runs/d694-intel-01/probes/frontier-3943001.probe.test.ts`, outputs `probe-full-fe991ace.json` / `probe-full-10f99026.json`): `engine.get_turn_context` on arena seed 3943001 — at 0a209799 (pre-B7) and fe991ace (B7 + fix r1) the team frontier is `contains_unresolved` with BOTH candidates `unresolved`, `reason_codes ['attack_allocation_unresolved']`, `unresolved_metrics ['lethality']`; at 10f99026 (fix r2) both are `resolved` with lethality 4939/1,000,000. So the pin at snippets.test.ts:369 (present since be09e575, introduced by de88050f) flipped because fix r2 removed `compareAllocations` from the actor-local path and computed lethality by an independent convolution of cached damage distributions (`combinedKillMillionths`, BigInt helpers) — a kill probability the allocation engine had refused to produce is now reported to the model. That is the "plausible value where the engine says unknown" failure §4 forbids; codex's hard stop was correct and its diagnosis ("stale pin; exactness") was wrong. FINDING AGAINST MY OWN BRIEF: fix r2's brief said "carry each actor's own local through allocation and aggregation" but did not say the allocation ENGINE must be preserved, and the manifest lacked `engine-query-port.ts`, where the allocation lives — so codex took the only in-manifest route, which was the wrong one. RULINGS: (a) 10f99026 is a BLOCKED candidate, not accepted; (b) B7 manifest AMENDED (D800 precedent) with `src/vtt/engine-query-port.ts` + `tests/unit/vtt/engine-query-port.test.ts` so an actor-local allocation variant (pre-resolved cached options + local mechanics, shared core with the host variant, no regeneration) can exist; (c) the independent convolution is deleted; lethality comes from allocation results; the snippets pin stays `contains_unresolved` and becomes an explicit witness in engine-mcp-server.test.ts; fully-perceived local == host frontier INCLUDING lethality is the equivalence proof; (d) fix r3 is the last B7 round before owner escalation. Brief staged: `.tmp/runs/d694-intel-01/impl-b7-fix-r3.md` (dispatch when codex reopens 2026-09-22 17:42). My verify of 10f99026 (`verify-b7-fix-r2.log`) continues for the record only. Next free id: D841.
.claude/decisions.md:1327:## D841 — OWNER (2026-09-21 08:26): DATA-01 Luna labelling hard cap = $500 total
.claude/decisions.md:1329:Verbatim: "500" to the question "what total hard spending limit for Luna labelling, pilot and retries included: $300 (codex) or $500 (supervisor recommendation)?". Ruling: the DATA-01 hard cap is **$500 total**, inclusive of the 200-state pilot, retries, ambiguity re-asks and recollection, with the plan's stop-before-cap rule (plan item 11) binding. The cost band in the plan ($55.50–$285 per 5,000 states at Luna list price, reasoning billed as output) fits under the cap with headroom for the pilot to settle the reasoning-length term. The DATA-01 plan's owner-input placeholder for the cap is to be filled in the next fix round (after astra r2, dispatch on codex reopen 2026-09-22 17:42). Next owner question (one at a time): the DM style Luna should imitate when labelling (recommendation: strongest legal monster tactics). Next free id: D842.
