.claude/decisions.md:1397:Verbatim: "I authorize a plan for this split as its own unit once the numbers are verified". Ruling as read: (1) D632's exclusion of "conversation optimization" and the vis-field brainstorm's rank 8 "not recommended, requires owner approval" are lifted for THIS mechanism only: whole tests move verbatim into ~4 files, every multi-round session chain kept whole; no test is cut, skipped, retimed or re-pinned. (2) Precondition: the supervisor's own measurement must confirm the shape — the quiet instrumented full gate and the --maxWorkers=1 verbose run of the file (chain running since 13:54, `.tmp/runs/test-perf/baseline-main/`) must show the file bounding the gate (file wall ≈ gate wall, other workers idle) and supply per-test durations for the balance. If the shape does not hold, stop and report; no plan. (3) The plan is a NEW unit (CONV-SPLIT-01), separate from TEST-PERF-01, codex-authored (sol high), astra HIGH review, ≤3 rounds; it inherits TEST-PERF-01 §1 evidence rules (AST title-multiset + modifier + expect/throw + timeout inventory, per-file declareTestInputs/hook ownership under isolate:false, immutable shared helpers, D583 GROUPS inventory under the demonstrate-then-normalize digest exception ONLY for the filename-set change) and §8 quiet-box acceptance, with acceptance measured on the FULL gate (A/A + three alternating pairs) since that is where the saving is claimed. (4) Dispatch when codex reopens (2026-09-22 17:42 EDT), after the numbers are in hand; order relative to TEST-PERF-01 B1 to be set by the supervisor (recommendation: CONV-SPLIT-01 plan first, it is the prize). Next owner question (one at a time): DATA-01 Opus judge hard cap (rec. $750). Next free id: D850.
