.claude/decisions.md:1762:LUNA6-01 plan review r1 (gpt-5.6-sol high, read-only, fresh; exit 0): REVISE 4 P1 / 4 P2 / 2 P3 — v7 not selectable by the operator CLIs and the first-arm validator would apply v5 provenance to v7 rows; the D569 registry test wrongly marked unchanged; the latency pilot censors at 900 s against an observed 902.7 s maximum; the mutation plan lacks exact killers. The reviewer confirmed the DATA-01 arithmetic ($500/33,801 = $0.01479246) and the v5 manifest/provenance hashes. Plan fix r1 goes to an Opus agent (D885 §7), then sol r2.
.claude/decisions.md:1764:1. D881 and D885 §8b say X2's projected-movement memo "never hit". The X2 hit audit I had fixed wrote counts only from a process 'exit' handler, and the vitest worker hit lines were lost: the audit file has no survival-scale block (roadmap agent read it; 0 projectedMovementState lines). Survival repeats the identical projected-movement computation 4,942 times per 30-seed run (ai-search, instrumented). The owner's drop decision stands for a different reason: AI-1 (ask once per decision) replaces the memo.
.claude/decisions.md:1768:Next free id: D888.
.claude/decisions.md:1771:## D888 — 2026-09-24 10:30 — Owner rulings (small units batched for timing; cover self-body bug fixed as its own unit; X1r also converts reachableCommandPaths); landing candidates built and reviewed; DATA-01 r4 REJECT (regressions) → owner; LUNA6 r2 REVISE
.claude/decisions.md:1774:1. Timing pairs → "Batch small exact units": units with identical pins that save under ~10 s each land in batches with one timed A/B pair per batch; big levers (reachable cells, board, cover walk, split, X3) keep their own pair. Amends D885 §6.
.claude/decisions.md:1775:2. Cover self-body bug → "Fix as its own unit". Confirmed in code by me: src/combat/cover.ts traceCombatantLine/traceCombatantLineToCells pass sourceId to traceSpaces (:502-503, :525), which never reads it; exclusions are only source+target cells (:427), so from a hypothetical anchor the mover's current body counts as creature cover. Output changes, so changed pins must be demonstrated row by row before any expectation changes. Opus agent building it (wf_6ceb79bc-f3a, unit coverself).
.claude/decisions.md:1781:- regex (lookbehind 8c28952f + parse-cache delete 62a3e621): APPROVE 0/0/1. P3: deleting the cache costs about 2.2 s on a one-worker tests/unit/simulation pass (22.6 → 24.8 s). SUPERVISOR DISPOSITION: land the delete anyway — owner's aim "remove the need for as many caches as is practical" (D885), 1,053 lines removed, cold derivation 169 ms; the cost is recorded here.
.claude/decisions.md:1784:- ai1: REVISE 0/3/0 (movement now computed before any command is assessed — verified by me in the diff; call count not tested directly; mutation evidence lacked per-mutant compilation and enforced killer names).
.claude/decisions.md:1785:- cachedel (6 commits): REVISE 0/2/1, all on 6ec4c2d2 (COMPILER_SNAPSHOTS: durationMs telemetry changes; +0.24–1.05 s on experiment-orchestrator vs a 0.5 s bar). SUPERVISOR DISPOSITION: drop 6ec4c2d2 and KEEP COMPILER_SNAPSHOTS — measured speed gain (≈84 ms per type-check) outweighs its memory (3.17 MB now, ≤34 MB) under D885 §9. The other five deletions stand.
.claude/decisions.md:1787:- board: REVISE 0/1/1 (the added independent-execution assertions have no exact-killer mutants).
.claude/decisions.md:1790:VERIFIED by me on a stack of x1r+ai1+cachedel+regex+x4+board over main (dnd-probe-verifystack-*, 13 commits, clean cherry-picks): `npx tsc -b --force` exit 0; all 7 D880 pins byte-identical; the 9 changed/new test files 107/107 (including the two docs files that fail on main).
.claude/decisions.md:1791:DATA-01 review r4 (gpt-5.6-sol high, fresh, read-only; archived plan .claude/consensus/data-01/plan-r4.md, 334 lines, sha 067aedba…): REJECT 0 P1 / 4 P2 / 0 P3. r3 P2-1, P2-3, P2-4, P2-5, P3-1, P3-2 CLOSED; P2-2 PARTIAL (the teacher agreement gate has no tuning scope). Three P2s are REGRESSIONS: fix r3 dropped previously closed text (format-selection contract when complete ranking is invalid; enriched-audit overlap/replenishment; family-disjoint audit and training-seed count). No round 5 without the owner (D885 §12a) → owner question.
.claude/decisions.md:1792:LUNA6-01 review r2 (gpt-5.6-sol high): REVISE 3 P1 / 3 P2 / 1 P3; r1 P1-1..P1-3, P2-1, P3-1, P3-2 CLOSED, four PARTIAL. SUPERVISOR READINGS of D887 given to the fix agent (not owner rulings): live escalation under an xhigh base = a fresh gpt-6-luna xhigh session; the two medium quality gates are script-chosen → xhigh; the codex explore route in the global CLAUDE.md is a codex helper, outside D887. Plan fix r2 running (same workflow as coverself).
