.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r1.log:1045:.claude/decisions.md:712:Verbatim: "b" (to the question "how much does the monster side know about a PC it has never perceived?", options A omniscience-always / B perceived-only / C encounter-level omniscience with actor-level ignorance). Ruling: a PC the monster has never perceived contributes nothing to monster planning or advice beyond its existence on the opposing roster (name/id). D418.1's capability/resource omniscience (exact AC, HP, slots, spell availability, rescue/revive) applies once the PC has been perceived by that actor's knowledge projection (seen, or held in observation history / search memory). Positions of unseen PCs remain unknown as before. This narrows D418.1 and confirms the D691 privacy invariance (request bytes invariant under unseen-PC relocation/speed/Paralyzed/absent-token variants) as the permanent contract, not a BLIND-01 interim. Effect on work in flight: none; B4 privacy pins stand; B6/B7 inherit. The Part A intel line and the Open-conflicts (verify) entry are updated in place below. Next free id: D695.
