.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:7433:- **P1 — D569 v7 is not operationally selectable, and the first-arm validator would apply v5 provenance rules to new v7 rows.** The plan proposes a version union and a `version → {primaryComparison, firstArm}` map ([plan:238](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:238)), but both operator CLIs still load the single v5 path: [d569-blind-experiment.ts:24](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tools/d569-blind-experiment.ts:24), [analyze-primary-pair.ts:154](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tools/d569-v5/analyze-primary-pair.ts:154), and [validate-first-arm.ts:277](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tools/d569-v5/validate-first-arm.ts:277). More seriously, the validator requires the historical original commit for most hard cells and the patched commit for only three replacements ([validate-first-arm.ts:307](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tools/d569-v5/validate-first-arm.ts:307)); fresh v7 rows should all have v7 provenance. Specify either separate immutable `tools/d569-v7` operators or an explicit, fail-closed manifest/version selector, plus version-specific row-contract and commit rules. Keep the installed v5 scripts byte-frozen: their hashes exactly match the launch provenance.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:7435:- **P1 — The D569 test touch-point census incorrectly marks the shared registry test unchanged.** The plan says `d569-blind-experiment.test.ts` stays untouched ([plan:76](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:76)), while B3 renames current constants under `D569_V5_*` and changes the schema to a version union ([plan:238](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:238)). That test imports the unversioned constants ([test:3](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tests/unit/tools/d569-blind-experiment.test.ts:3)), declares only the v5 manifest as input ([test:97](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tests/unit/tools/d569-blind-experiment.test.ts:97)), and asserts those constants are the v5 literals ([test:412](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tests/unit/tools/d569-blind-experiment.test.ts:412)). It must be included in B3 unless the implementation preserves obsolete aliases, which conflicts with the project’s replace-freely rule.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:7437:- **P1 — The latency pilot is not actually uncensored.** It chooses a 900-second timeout while citing an observed maximum of 902.7 seconds ([plan:189](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:189), [plan:393](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:393)), and then derives the budget from successful sessions only ([plan:193](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:193)). Any slower xhigh calls are censored and excluded, biasing p95 downward. Predeclare that any pilot timeout withholds the budget, or use a censored-data rule; do not call 900 seconds uncensoring.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:7439:- **P1 — The mutation plan does not meet the binding exact-killer protocol.** Decisions require a named compiling runtime mutation, exact killer, reachability evidence, guarded scripts, and exact-byte restoration ([decisions.md:88](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.claude/decisions.md:88)). M1/M2 cite “route test” and “same set”; M6/M11 name only prospective generic tests; no exact test titles, mutation commands, changed-line/count assertions, reachability checks, or restoration procedure are specified ([plan:126](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:126)). M5 must unconditionally add a whitespace/raw-byte mutant and a literal SHA test—no existing test pins the manifest’s raw SHA. Add mutants for v7 manifest selection, v7 commit provenance, wrong non-Luna effort, wrong v7 wall, and v5/v7 cross-selection.
