.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:7443:- **P2 — DATA-01 arithmetic is correct, but the operational cost gate is incomplete.** I independently reproduced all four sensitivity rows and the exact break-evens: `$500/33,801 = $0.01479246` and `$500/5,801 = $0.08619204`. Current official standard short-context pricing is `$0.10/M` input and `$0.50/M` output; at 12k input, 8k/16k/24k/32k caps reserve `$0.0052/$0.0092/$0.0132/$0.0172`, producing maximum-pilot costs of `$175.77/$310.97/$446.17/$581.38`. However, pricing also varies by processing tier and region, so `pricingVersion` must pin tier, region, and route—not merely model prices. Additionally, “fits under $500” at the mathematical break-even leaves no reserve for retries or ambiguous holds, although D841 includes them. Define mandatory headroom before authorizing the pilot. [Official GPT-6 Luna documentation](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-luna).
