.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:7470:- **P1 — The D569 test touch-point census incorrectly marks the shared registry test unchanged.** The plan says `d569-blind-experiment.test.ts` stays untouched ([plan:76](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:76)), while B3 renames current constants under `D569_V5_*` and changes the schema to a version union ([plan:238](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:238)). That test imports the unversioned constants ([test:3](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tests/unit/tools/d569-blind-experiment.test.ts:3)), declares only the v5 manifest as input ([test:97](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tests/unit/tools/d569-blind-experiment.test.ts:97)), and asserts those constants are the v5 literals ([test:412](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tests/unit/tools/d569-blind-experiment.test.ts:412)). It must be included in B3 unless the implementation preserves obsolete aliases, which conflicts with the project’s replace-freely rule.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:7472:- **P1 — The latency pilot is not actually uncensored.** It chooses a 900-second timeout while citing an observed maximum of 902.7 seconds ([plan:189](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:189), [plan:393](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:393)), and then derives the budget from successful sessions only ([plan:193](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-draft.md:193)). Any slower xhigh calls are censored and excluded, biasing p95 downward. Predeclare that any pilot timeout withholds the budget, or use a censored-data rule; do not call 900 seconds uncensoring.
