.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8934:- Non-Luna D569 arms remain high.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8938:- D887 says every script-chosen live-play Luna run moves to xhigh ([decisions.md:1752](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.claude/decisions.md:1752)), but r2 leaves live escalation open to xhigh, max, removal, or high ([plan-r2.md:433-438](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:433)).
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8939:- r2 acknowledges the two medium quality gates are script-chosen and therefore read as xhigh, but still offers medium/both alternatives ([plan-r2.md:439-443](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:439)).
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8940:- The actual live migration is delegated to unspecified external “run wrappers” ([plan-r2.md:47](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:47), [plan-r2.md:388](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:388)). No wrapper inventory, frozen argv, conversation/escalation smoke, or guard proves that every future live run selects the required route.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8941:- Q8 remains an unresolved classification of an explicitly script/config-chosen Luna route. The plan must either place it outside D887 with a concrete rationale or apply D887; leaving it indeterminate prevents an exact-scope claim.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8947:- **D887’s settled live-play scope is reopened, while the actual wrapper migration is unverifiable.** The options in Q1 and Q9 permit lower effort, max effort, or removal despite D887’s “every script-chosen Luna run … live play” ruling. Meanwhile, code defaults deliberately remain Sol and wrapper work is only named generically. V13 proves one arena invocation, not the live conversation, speculation, correction and escalation surfaces ([plan-r2.md:411](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:411)). Resolve D887 directly, enumerate the new wrapper artifacts and their exact argv, and add both arena and conversation/escalation route witnesses.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8949:- **The v7 independent-pin sequence is circular.** B3 includes the fixture, raw-SHA constant and T3 tests ([plan-r2.md:387](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:387)); the D-entry is not written until Phase 4 ([plan-r2.md:388](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:388)); yet the constant and test pin must be copied from that D-entry ([plan-r2.md:318-324](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:318)). Split this into: hand-author and V9-review fixture → independently record hashes/amendments → implement constants/operators/tests from the recorded entry.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8951:- **M21 and M22 lack exact killers.** For M21, changing the v7 path to the v5 path still satisfies the named negative test “v7 operators refuse the v5 manifest” ([plan-r2.md:180](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:180)); the mutant can survive. It needs a positive v7-operator acceptance test that necessarily reads the registered v7 path. For M22, a generic row that differs from launch provenance can be rejected by both the correct and mutated validators ([plan-r2.md:181](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:181)). Freeze a witness whose row commit equals `D569_ORIGINAL_COMMIT` while provenance names a different v7 launch commit, so only the mutant accepts it.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8955:- **DATA-01’s arithmetic uses a superseded denominator.** r2 labels 33,801 as the “Max pilot” and derives `$0.01479246` ([plan-r2.md:336-351](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:336)). The revised DATA-01 ledger is 34,801 scheduled requests and 50,801 at the absolute 60-attempt envelope ([plan-r4.md:125-147](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.claude/consensus/data-01/plan-r4.md:125)). Therefore:
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8963:- **V6 and V10 do not provide one executable frozen-file rule.** V6 unconditionally requires `ai-dm-arena.test.ts` to be byte-identical ([plan-r2.md:404](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:404)), while V10 may append tests there and substitutes `git diff --numstat: 0 deleted lines` ([plan-r2.md:408](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:408)). Zero deletions proves additive changes, not that additions occurred only at the intended describe boundary. Specify mutually exclusive commands and an AST/title-preservation or exact-prefix/suffix check.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8965:- **External timeout provenance is asserted but not tested.** The resolver prints `{timeoutMs, source}`, and wrappers are expected to copy it into provenance ([plan-r2.md:235](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:235)), but no wrapper schema, fixture, exact assertion or mutant covers that transfer. This is particularly important because row-level recording was deliberately dropped. Make the wrapper/provenance artifact concrete and give the copy operation a named runtime mutant and exact killer.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8969:- **V13 permits a smoke that bypasses the table it nominally checks.** It accepts either a table timeout or explicit `1,800,000` ms ([plan-r2.md:411](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:411)). The latter proves only `cli_override`, not that the measured xhigh entry is wired. Keep an early explicit-timeout availability probe, but require the post-B1b smoke to omit `--timeout-ms` and prove `route_table:<D-id>`.
.tmp/runs/luna6/review-r2.log:8973:The historical boundary is substantially improved: v5 fixture bytes, installed scripts, patched in-repo operators, tests and D880 pins are all separately preserved. The pilot now has a predeclared budget rule, withholds on censoring, measures by effort/path and forbids load-driven re-pinning. The no-flag defaults have independent historical oracles rather than regenerated expectations. The DATA-01 price basis is properly marked unverified, and tier/region/route/headroom are now recognized as part of the cost contract.
