   141	### 2.2 Mutation protocol (r1 P1-4)
   142	
   143	This follows Part A :88. Every mutant runs on a clean checkout of the candidate SHA under `PhpstormProjects`, through `slot.sh`. Each has a guarded script, `.tmp/runs/luna6/impl/<batch>/mutate.mjs <id>`, that does the following:
   144	
   145	1. Records the target's sha256 (ORIG).
   146	2. Runs the killer unmutated: `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --configLoader runner --maxWorkers=1 <file> -t '<title>'`. The script regex-escapes the title, because `-t` is a pattern and titles contain `(`, `)` and `.`. It must exit 0 and report exactly one test as passed; a skipped or filtered-out test fails the step.
   147	3. Applies an exact-string replacement that must match **exactly once**. It fails loudly on 0 or more than 1 match, and prints `CHANGED <file>:<line>: <old> -> <new> (1)`.
   148	4. For a code mutant, runs `npx tsc -b --force` and requires exit 0, because a type-rejected mutant proves nothing at runtime. Fixture mutants skip this step.
   149	5. Runs the killer again, teed to `<id>.log`. A **kill** requires three things: a non-zero exit, the named test listed as failed, and an assertion diff or violation list that contains the mutated value (this is the reachability evidence). A crash, import error, timeout or skip is **not** a kill (see the memory notes on Stryker import crashes and exit codes).
   150	6. Writes the saved original bytes back, requires sha256 = ORIG, and prints `RESTORED <sha>`.
   151	
   152	The implementer runs all mutants and the supervisor re-runs them. The kill evidence is read from the logs.
