   237	### 3.4 Pilot (supervisor-run; quiet box per D883; never re-pinned for load)
   238	
   239	- **P0 route probes, one call each.**
   240	  - (a) `CODEX_HOME=/home/vagrant/.codex-aidm codex exec -m gpt-6-luna -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh --sandbox read-only -` on the stale-cache path used by the screenshot probe.
   241	  - (b) One arena round with `--cli codex --model gpt-6-luna --effort xhigh --timeout-ms 1800000` through an isolated home. This is the arena path, and it also confirms the §3.1 wall behaviour.
   242	- **P1 arms are conditional on the rulings (r1 P2-1).** Every model/effort/path combination that will actually run gets measured evidence before it gets a budget. An unpiloted combination has no table entry, so the resolver fails closed (§3.3).
   243	
   244	| Arm | Route | Paths piloted | Needed because |
   245	|---|---|---|---|
   246	| A | gpt-6-luna xhigh | legacy (arena advice), dm_mode (blind), screenshot (if Q9 = a or c) | live play, D569 v7, gates |
   247	| B | gpt-6-luna medium | legacy; screenshot (if Q9 = b or c) | D484 loop; gates under Q9 b/c |
   248	| C | gpt-6-luna low | legacy; screenshot only if a low screenshot study is scheduled | generate-data K6, D425, D449, :456 research arm |
   249	| D | gpt-6-luna max | legacy | only if Q1 = (b) |
   250	| E | gpt-5.6-luna medium | legacy | optional continuity with the 4-5/30 note; **no budget derived** |
   251	
   252	- **Sample.** Per arm and path: 30 day-1 sessions (10 fixed rooms × 3 reps), interleaved across arms by cell, plus a 10-session day-2 slice. The sample is **every session that returned a model response**, whatever its outcome (authorized, refused or validation failure). Sessions classified `infrastructure_failed` are excluded and listed. If more than 10 % of an arm/path is infrastructure failures, that arm/path is void and rerun. Durations come from rollout first and last events, copied out of `/tmp` immediately, plus per-round `endToEndWall`, reasoning and output tokens, outcome, and fractions over 120/180/240 s.
   253	- **Censoring (r1 P1-3).** The pilot timeout is **T = 1,800 s**, 2× the longest codex session ever seen in `~/.codex-aidm` (902.7 s [V-r0]). The draft's 900 s was below that maximum. The rule is fixed before P1: **if any session in an arm/path reaches T, that arm/path's budget is withheld** and the owner is told. No budget is ever derived from a censored sample. After the second T-hit, that arm/path stops early to save wall time.
   254	- **Budget rule (fixed before P1).** Take the pooled n = 40 sample and its nearest-rank p95, which is the 38th order statistic [V: `ceil(0.95·40) = 38`]. The budget is the smallest multiple of 30 s that is ≥ 1.25 × p95. Stability check: if the day-1-only p95 (29th of 30) and the pooled p95 differ by more than 20 %, the budget is withheld. The report states the fraction of pilot sessions the budget would have cut. With n = 40, the p95 rests on 2-3 order statistics, and the report says so.
   255	- **Live round wall.** It is not derived. If A-legacy shows p95 `endToEndWall` > 180 s, ask Q2 with the numbers.
   256	- **Cost and wall.** Usage is codex-plan only [V-r0]. Wall time is at least 6.65 h serial if xhigh ≈ gpt-5.6-luna high's 162 s, or about 12.1 h if xhigh takes twice as long [I; node arithmetic, Appendix A]. It runs over two days because of the day-2 slice.
   257	- **Order.** The screenshot path runs after B1 lands, because it needs `--timeout-ms`. All other paths can run before any code lands, with an explicit `--timeout-ms 1800000`.
