## D887 scope

As literally asked, **plan-r2 does not implement exactly D887**. It leaves live escalation, both quality gates, and the explore route unresolved and delegates live migration to unspecified wrappers ([plan-r2.md:433](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:433), [plan-r2.md:439](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:439), [plan-r2.md:450](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:450)).

At the route-selection level, **plan-r3 matches D887 and the supplied D888 readings**:

- script-chosen game Luna routes become gpt-6-luna/xhigh;
- effort studies retain low/medium;
- the Sol/medium no-flag default and legacy pins remain unchanged;
- the global Codex explore helper remains outside scope;
- non-Luna D569 arms remain high.

That scope is neither broadened nor narrowed. Its runtime implementation is nevertheless unproved because of the deadline defect below.

## Findings

### P1

- **The pilot, live route, and D569 v7 wall are all capped at 180 seconds, contradicting the plan’s central uncensored-budget premise.** r3 asserts that “the round wall does not abort the primary session” and that V13a confirms this ([plan-r3.md:303](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:303)); it then derives budgets from a nominal 1,800-second uncensored pilot ([plan-r3.md:324](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:324)). Actual code fixes the round wall at 180,000 ms ([ai-dm-arena.ts:423](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tools/ai-dm-arena.ts:423), [ai-dm-conversation.ts:1265](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tools/ai-dm-conversation.ts:1265)), creates the primary dispatch deadline from it ([ai-dm-conversation.ts:5544](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/tools/ai-dm-conversation.ts:5544)), and clamps the invocation timeout to the remaining round deadline ([agent-session-lifecycle.ts:64](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/src/vtt/agent-session-lifecycle.ts:64), [agent-session-lifecycle.ts:157](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/src/vtt/agent-session-lifecycle.ts:157)). Therefore responses above 180 seconds are aborted/censored long before T=1,800 seconds. The same defect makes the D569 v7 runbook’s registered wall—always at least 240,000 ms—ineffective ([plan-r3.md:169](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:169), [plan-r3.md:536](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:536)). This requires a dedicated uncensored latency harness or an explicitly authorized pilot/experiment round-wall design, plus an effective-timeout witness at the adapter boundary.

- **Q4a(ii) cannot produce truthful v7 provenance.** Amendment #6 remains frozen as saying fixtures and caps are carried unchanged from v5 ([plan-r2.md:289](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r2.md:289), carried forward at [plan-r3.md:375](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:375)). Yet Q4a(ii) permits waiting for COHORT v6 ([plan-r3.md:527](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:527)), while S4 unconditionally writes v7 “from the v5 bytes” ([plan-r3.md:392](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:392)). Either remove option ii or condition the source manifest, diff allowlist, amendment #6, V9, and hash provenance on the owner’s answer.

- **The mutation contract is still not met for the launcher’s runtime safety.** Decisions require a compiling runtime mutant and exact killer for each load-bearing assertion ([decisions.md:88](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.claude/decisions.md:88)). M39’s mutation emits a real side-effect import under `verbatimModuleSyntax`, but its killer merely scans source text ([plan-r3.md:270](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:270)); it never proves that the runner auto-main path is or is not reached. Likewise, the provenance file’s no-overwrite guarantee has no `wx → w` mutant, despite being relied upon as immutable launch evidence ([plan-r3.md:346](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:346)).

- **DATA-01 authorization is contradictory.** r3 correctly records that DATA-01 r4 is rejected and that round 5 requires the owner ([plan-r3.md:418](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:418); [decisions.md:1791](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.claude/decisions.md:1791)), but then says that if cost tests S and A pass the pilot is “authorized under the existing rulings” ([plan-r3.md:440](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:440)). Later it again says residuals block DATA-01’s paid pilot ([plan-r3.md:459](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:459)). Passing S/A may clear only the cost condition; it cannot authorize a paid pilot while the governing plan is rejected.

### P2

- **The headroom formula mixes dollars and percentages.** The plan writes `r ≤ (500 − H) / N` but then supplies “H = 10%” and “H = 20%” ([plan-r3.md:433](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:433)). The printed numbers actually use `$500 × (1 − h) / N`. Define either fractional `h` with that formula or dollar reserve `H_dollars` with `(500 − H_dollars)/N`. The numeric results themselves are correct.

- **The T7b oracle derives its expected array length from observed production output.** It proposes an all-xhigh literal “of the observed length,” followed only by `length >= 3` ([plan-r3.md:275](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:275)). That is weaker than an independently pinned phase/call sequence and permits missing or duplicate invocations once three remain. It also fails to provide the runtime double-start killer M39 needs. Pin the expected invocation phases/count independently for each witness.

- **The launcher’s stated process contract is incompletely verified.** The plan promises checkout cwd, inherited stdio, and propagation of the child exit code ([plan-r3.md:160](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:160)), but T7a is specified only around command arrays, route flags, provenance ordering, and refusal behavior. Add exact injected-spawner assertions and named mutants for cwd, stdio, and exit-code propagation.

### P3

- **Several “exact” gates are still indirect references rather than self-contained commands.** V5 says “the r2 V5 command,” V8 says “the r2 V8 command,” and V12 says “as in r2” ([plan-r3.md:492](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:492), [plan-r3.md:496](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:496), [plan-r3.md:501](/home/vagrant/PhpstormProjects/dnd-multiclass-spells-static/.tmp/runs/luna6/plan-r3.md:501)). Before approval, copy the authoritative commands and pass criteria into r3 so the final plan is executable without reconstructing an earlier revision.

